# Practical: Build a Jenkins Pipeline for GitHub Integration

We'll build a simple pipeline that does this:

```text
GitHub
   ↓
Jenkins
   ↓
Clone repository
   ↓
Build/Test
   ↓
Show SUCCESS
```

Then we'll configure a **GitHub webhook** so that a push to GitHub can automatically trigger Jenkins.

A Jenkins Pipeline is normally defined in a `Jenkinsfile` stored in your source-control repository. Jenkins recommends this "Pipeline as code" approach. [Jenkins](https://www.jenkins.io/doc/pipeline/tour/hello-world/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

