# Step 14 — Connect GitHub to Jenkins using a Webhook

Now we'll make it automatic.

Instead of manually clicking:

```text
Build Now
```

we want:

```text
GitHub Push
      ↓
GitHub Webhook
      ↓
Jenkins
      ↓
Pipeline automatically runs
```

Jenkins' GitHub plugin supports triggering jobs when changes are pushed to GitHub. [Jenkins Plugins](https://plugins.jenkins.io/github/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

---

# Step 15 — Configure Jenkins webhook trigger

Open:

```text
Jenkins
→ GitHub-Demo-Pipeline
→ Configure
```

Find:

```text
Build Triggers
```

Select:

```text
GitHub hook trigger for GITScm polling
```

Save the configuration.

This trigger is the Jenkins mechanism commonly used for GitHub push webhooks. [Jenkins Plugins](https://plugins.jenkins.io/github/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

---

# Step 16 — Add the webhook in GitHub

Open your GitHub repository:

```text
git-demo
```

Go to:

```text
Settings
    ↓
Webhooks
    ↓
Add webhook
```

For the payload URL, use:

```text
http://YOUR-JENKINS-ADDRESS/github-webhook/
```

For a Jenkins server exposed at a public address, it could look like:

```text
https://jenkins.example.com/github-webhook/
```

The Jenkins GitHub plugin documents the webhook endpoint in the form:

```text
$JENKINS_BASE_URL/github-webhook/
``` :chatgpt-content-reference{index="7"}


Set:

```text
Content type:
application/json
```

For events, select:

```text
Just the push event
```

Then click:

```text
Add webhook
```

---

## ⚠️ Important if Jenkins is running on your own PC

If Jenkins is running at:

```text
http://localhost:8080
```

GitHub's servers **cannot normally reach your `localhost` directly**.

This will not work as a GitHub webhook URL:

```text
http://localhost:8080/github-webhook/
```

For a real GitHub → Jenkins webhook, Jenkins needs to be reachable by GitHub over the network, usually through a properly configured public/hosted Jenkins endpoint.

For your college practical, you can first demonstrate the integration with **Build Now**, and then configure the webhook when your Jenkins instance has a reachable URL.

